WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.168
-Yeah, you know,
things are good.

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.569
I mean, we're back
in the studio.

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:05.004
We're live tonight,
which is cool,

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:07.106
but there's barely
anyone here.

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:08.741
It's a little weird.

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:11.377
-I know, man, it's like, we're
getting back to normal.

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:13.279
But at the same time,
not at all.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.914
-Yeah, exactly.

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.616
But you know the one thing
I would love

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:17.917
more than anything?

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.553
Is to have a guest in person.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:23.456
I miss talking to someone
in person.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.091
-Yeah, man, I know
what you're saying.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:27.292
I just miss being in the same
room with other people,

00:00:27.292 --> 00:00:29.095
you know?
-Right?

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.897
-What's up, John?
-Hey, Jimmy, what's up?

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:40.006
[ Both screaming ]

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:42.008
[ Bouncy theme music playing ]

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:49.549
♪♪

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:55.221
♪♪

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.890
-Live from Rockefeller Center
in the heart of New York City,

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:00.993
it's "The Tonight Show
Starring Jimmy Fallon."

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:03.229
Tonight, join Jimmy
and his guests

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.831
John Cena,

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.866
musical guest BTS,

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.035
and featuring the
Legendary Roots Crew.

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:10.937
♪♪

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:14.073
And now here's your host --
Jimmy Fallon.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:15.508
♪♪

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:16.509
-Get it!

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:21.814
♪♪

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:24.583
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:26.819
-Oh!

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:30.690
Yes!
Hello!

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.026
Thank you very much.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:01:34.026 --> 00:01:37.596
You guys,
we are live right now.

00:01:37.596 --> 00:01:41.968
We are live from New York City!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:46.606
And man,
what the hell was that...

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.607
debate?
Was that debate?

00:01:48.607 --> 00:01:51.444
What did we -- I am so --

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:54.214
What was that?

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:57.016
I am so stressed right now.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:59.451
I have a kink.
It just --

00:01:59.451 --> 00:02:01.421
I felt like I just slept on
an air mattress.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.589
Just one of those kinks
that just --

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:04.991
I got to get psyched.

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:06.925
We do have a great show tonight.

00:02:06.925 --> 00:02:10.496
John Cena is here in the studio.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:12.331
First live guest in the studio,

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:14.367
John Cena, we love him.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.570
Also, we have music from BTS
every single...

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.971
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:21.407
...night this week,
we're having some performance

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:22.841
from BTS, it's gonna be good.

00:02:22.841 --> 00:02:26.979
I'm actually pumped.
I am so amped right now,

00:02:26.979 --> 00:02:28.881
President Trump demanded
I take a drug test.

00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:31.383
That's how...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.383 --> 00:02:33.519
Well, guys,
tonight in Cleveland,

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:35.354
it was the first
presidential debate

00:02:35.354 --> 00:02:37.856
between President Trump
and Vice President Joe Biden.

00:02:37.856 --> 00:02:40.927
And boy, wasn't that fun?

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:44.596
Seriously, did anyone take
anything away from tonight?

00:02:44.596 --> 00:02:47.399
Was that helpful
to any American?

00:02:47.399 --> 00:02:49.602
The only person enjoyed that
was Vladimir Putin

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.270
while he was stroking a cat.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:55.908
"Yes. Yes, yes."
[ Laughs ]

00:02:55.908 --> 00:02:57.877
Honestly, sitting through
that debate felt like

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:00.713
getting a COVID test
in both nostrils at once.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:01.714
I was like...

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:03.616
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.918
Seriously, after the debate,
I threw on "The Vow"

00:03:05.918 --> 00:03:07.553
just to pick myself up.

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:08.988
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.723
Things were tense tonight, man.

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.925
Usually when you see two guys
this age arguing,

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:16.896
it's about leaves blowing
on each other's lawn.

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:19.699
As expected, the debate was
full of hurtful insults,

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:22.301
constant fighting and
vicious personal attacks.

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:24.403
Or as Americans call it,
Thanksgiving.

00:03:24.403 --> 00:03:27.239
[ Laughter ]
Before the debate, Chris Wallace

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:28.808
said that if he does
his job right,

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:30.610
it'll be like he's not there.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.311
Well, mission accomplished.

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:33.913
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.881
Things got really ugly.

00:03:35.881 --> 00:03:38.618
After the debate was over,
Wallace said he wants to

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.420
moderate something a little
more civil

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:44.723
like a Real Housewives reunion
or a back alley knife fight.

00:03:44.723 --> 00:03:48.027
Tonight's debate was presented
without commercials.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.696
Yeah. The only interruptions
were Trump cutting off

00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:52.865
Biden and Chris Wallace
every eight seconds.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.233
[ Rapid stammering ]

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:57.370
"No, you're allowed...
[ Rapid stammering ]

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.771
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.439
No, you said I have to do --

00:04:00.439 --> 00:04:03.576
you have to do the --
I did what you said."

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:06.212
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:07.947
Actually tonight's debate
made history.

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:09.882
It was the first time Americans
ever watched something on TV

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.650
and wished there were
commercials.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:13.519
I need a break!

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:16.322
I break! Give me a gecko.
Give me something.

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:18.157
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.627
Things got brutal fast.
Just to give you an idea,

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:22.561
this was one of
the lighter moments.

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:24.063
-All right, gentlemen --

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.531
-Which was heavily --
-Mr. President --

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.966
-You would have been
much later, Joe.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.067
-Mr. President --
-Much later.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.235
Mr. President --
-You're talking about

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:31.871
2 million people.

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:34.173
-Chris Wallace felt like
a kindergarten teacher

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:37.009
running a class on Zoom.

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:39.378
And the night went downhill
pretty quickly.

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:41.313
Biden was doing everything
he could to try to

00:04:41.313 --> 00:04:43.715
get Trump to stop interrupting,
take a look at this.

00:04:43.715 --> 00:04:45.317
-Donald, would you just
be quiet for a minute?

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:46.819
-And you don't know her --
-Will you shut up, man?

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.621
-Who was -- Listen --
-This is so unpresidential.

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:49.688
-He's gonna pack the --

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:52.124
-Will he just shush
for a minute?

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:54.927
-After that, Biden got
a standing ovation from Melania.

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:57.663
It's like...
"Finally!

00:04:57.663 --> 00:04:59.531
Finally!
[ Applause ]

00:04:59.531 --> 00:05:01.567
Some --"

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.502
At that point, I was just
waiting for a woman in a bikini

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:06.172
to walk out holding a sign
that said "Round 2."

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:07.706
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.706 --> 00:05:09.942
You know it was a rough debate
when the guy who told

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:12.845
the president to shut up was
seen as the classy candidate.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.147
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:16.348
Well, the first of the night's
six sections

00:05:16.348 --> 00:05:19.551
was about the Supreme Court,
and it ended like this.

00:05:19.551 --> 00:05:20.986
Watch this exchange.

00:05:20.986 --> 00:05:22.922
-This is so unpresidential.
-He's gonna pack the Court.

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:25.324
-That was really a productive
segment, wasn't it?

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:26.692
[ Chuckling ]

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:28.127
Keep yapping, man.

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:32.699
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:36.969
Sadly, looking back, that was
the most productive segment.

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:39.872
After that, the debate moved on
to the pandemic.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:42.408
Then Biden tried to hit Trump
with a quick sound byte.

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:43.609
Watch this.

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:45.011
-When he was presented
with that number,

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:47.146
he said "It is what it is."

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:50.116
Well, it is what it is
because you are who you are.

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:53.952
-Ooh.

00:05:53.952 --> 00:05:56.556
-Even Dr. Seuss was like, "Wait,
what are we talking about?"

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:58.657
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.657 --> 00:06:02.695
"It is what... we are --
is what you are?"

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:04.330
But Biden couldn't talk
about the pandemic

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.698
without bringing up
one of Trump's

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.966
most famous gaffes.
Check it out.

00:06:07.966 --> 00:06:10.136
-This is the same man...
-It's all set up.

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:13.439
-...who told you by Easter,
this would be gone away.

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:15.340
By the warm weather,
it would be gone,

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:16.976
miraculously,
like a miracle.

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:19.211
By the way, maybe you could
inject some bleach in your arm

00:06:19.211 --> 00:06:20.712
and that would take care of it.

00:06:20.712 --> 00:06:22.214
This is the same man.
-That was said sarcastically.

00:06:22.214 --> 00:06:24.917
You know that.

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:26.919
-Meanwhile, a guy injecting
bleach into his arm

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:29.422
was like, "Wait, what do you
mean sarcastically?"

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:33.492
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.492 --> 00:06:36.262
Trump is like,
"I don't inject bleach.

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:38.931
I wear a patch and slowly
absorb it all day."

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:41.867
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.867 --> 00:06:43.703
At the end of Trump's
presidency, he'll just be like,

00:06:43.703 --> 00:06:46.973
"Come on, everything I said
was sarcastic.

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:49.575
Well, just...
[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:51.577
No, you said that, I...

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:53.946
No, no, well, you said --
I said..."

00:06:55.248 --> 00:06:56.882
Of course trump tried
to fight back.

00:06:56.882 --> 00:06:58.584
He really took issue with Biden
using the word smart.

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:00.853
Watch this.
-Unless he gets a lot smarter

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:03.455
a lot quicker --
-Mr. President?

00:07:03.455 --> 00:07:05.390
-Did you use
the word smart?

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:08.194
Don't use the word smart
with me.

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:12.731
[ Laughter ]

00:07:12.731 --> 00:07:15.200
Yep. Trump accused Biden
of not being smart.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.470
He was like, "I'm much smarter.
That's how is how I got

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.538
nominated for the
Taco Bell Peace Prize."

00:07:19.538 --> 00:07:22.675
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.675 --> 00:07:24.743
And finally, Biden had
really had enough

00:07:24.743 --> 00:07:26.312
and hit Trump with this insult.

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:28.313
-People out there need help.

00:07:28.313 --> 00:07:30.683
-But why didn't you do it
over the last 25 years?

00:07:30.683 --> 00:07:32.050
-Because you weren't
president --

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:33.385
-Why didn't you do it
over the last 25 years?

00:07:33.385 --> 00:07:34.954
-Because you weren't president
screwing things up.

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:37.056
-You were a Senator and --
-You're the worst president

00:07:37.056 --> 00:07:39.725
America has ever had.
Come on.

00:07:39.725 --> 00:07:41.093
-Oof.

00:07:41.093 --> 00:07:43.095
Trump was like,
"That's ridiculous.

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:44.563
Everyone knows I'm somewhere
between

00:07:44.563 --> 00:07:46.666
George Washington
and Martin Sheen."

00:07:46.666 --> 00:07:48.234
[ Laughter ]

